# engineering.local (project repo)

Selected upstream set:

- primary lane: `{%- if language == "python" -%}py{%- elif language in ["node", "typescript"] -%}ts{%- elif language == "go" -%}go{%- elif language == "rust" -%}rust{%- elif language == "elixir" -%}elixir{%- endif -%}`
- selected disciplines: start with `validation`, `testing`, `security-privacy`, `documentation`, and `dependency-governance`; add `local-first-data`, `observability`, `accessibility`, `design-system`, `specification-and-dsls`, `engineering-reasoning`, or `build-graph-acceleration` only when the repo concern requires them.
- `specification-and-dsls` is optional for schemas, generators, policy DSLs, or executable contracts; `engineering-reasoning` is optional for explicit decision/reasoning posture.
- `build-graph-acceleration` is optional/evidence-gated for Buck2, Bazel, Pants, Nx/Turborepo, remote cache, or remote execution work; native language tooling remains canonical unless repo-local acceptance says otherwise.
{%- if language == "rust" %}
- conditional Rust addendum: `rust-build-graph` only when Rust build/test time is a measured bottleneck; Cargo remains canonical and Buck2/Bazel are optional acceleration overlays, not default Rust requirements.
{%- endif %}
- executable upstream retrieval lives in `policy/engineering-lane.json` -> `engineering_core.command`; use `engineering_core.catalog_command`, `engineering_core.list_disciplines_command`, and `engineering_core.list_templates_command` to inspect newly available lanes, addenda, disciplines, templates, and profiles.

Executable contract surface:

- `policy/engineering-lane.json` declares the upstream lane reference, retrieval command, catalog/list commands, and scanner-visible selected disciplines.
- `docs/engineering.local.md` records repo-local selected disciplines and deltas.
- Repo validation should at least verify the declared lane metadata and may smoke the declared command when available.

Repo-local emphasis:

- This file is the local override layer on top of the upstream lane/discipline catalog.
- Keep workflow scripts and docs aligned with the declared lane contract.
- Prefer local deterministic wrappers before ad-hoc commands.
- Update this file when local practice intentionally diverges from the upstream lane or adopts a new discipline.
{%- endif -%}
